# Test: the declared distances apply when the config carries NO rib block.
# VALIDATES: AC-1 -- every protocol holds its declared distance with no config.
# PREVENTS: the regression an independent closure gate caught on 2026-09-04,
#           where the declaration reached nothing on an ordinary configuration.
#
# WHY THIS CASE EXISTS AND WHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY. The first version of this
# feature resolved the distance table only when a config section arrived, and
# ExtractConfigSubtree (internal/component/config/plugin_verify.go) returns nil
# for an absent path, so a config with no `rib {` block delivered NO section:
# publishDistances never ran and every producer stayed on its own constant
# permanently. Exactly ONE config in this repository carries a `rib {` block, so
# the defect was invisible to every other case in this suite.
#
# The daemon now seeds the declaration at plugin start (runSysRIBPlugin), so a
# config with no rib block is the case that must work, and this file is
# deliberately one that does not mention rib at all.

stdin=dist-no-rib:terminator=EOF_NORIB
bgp {
	session {
		asn {
			local 65000;
		}
	}
}
EOF_NORIB

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=dist-no-rib:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
